  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Dependencies**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the project\'s dependencies to understand the technology stack. Initial assessment reveals React 19, React-DOM 19, TailwindCSS v4, and Lucide-React 0.546. This initial scan will inform the planning, and help lay the groundwork for understanding the project\'s requirements.\n\n\n**Reviewing Package Versions**\n\nI\'ve updated my understanding of the technology stack to include motion 12.23.24, express 4.21.2, and vite 8.3.0. I\'m checking the artifact directory path for the implementation plan which appears to be located at `.aistudio/artifacts/brain/c00b0a3d-05f4-41fa-bc3d-91d1fccc33d7/implementation_plan.md`. This information, along with user requirements, will help to identify potential implementation gaps.\n\n\n**Exploring Cooking Oils**\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific oils, especially flaxseed and camellia seed oils. I\'m noting the ideal uses: raw consumption for flaxseed due to its Omega-3 richness and sensitivity to heat and light, and high-heat cooking versatility for camellia seed oil, thanks to its high smoke point and MUFA content. The selection guide considers pressing methods and packaging for quality.\n\n\n**Evaluating Oil Features**\n\nI am now carefully evaluating features of cooking oils to refine the knowledge base. This includes acid value and testing certifications, storage, expiration protocols, and sensory characteristics alongside labeling inspections. Additionally, I am curating evidence cards from respected sources like NEJM and AHA, offering filters for easy access. I\'m exploring an interactive \"Cooking Oil Matcher\" tool to help users select oils based on their cooking techniques and health objectives.\n\n\n**Defining Implementation Steps**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining implementation steps. This involves crafting interactive tools like a smoke point comparison chart with a temperature slider, an Omega ratio visualizer, and a top bar with a 3-zone contract. I am also planning the disclaimer section. I am now working on verifying the required `implementation_plan.md` template and structure, which includes the project name, goals, user review section, and detailed breakdowns of the overview, UX/design.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
